WEBVTT

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:11.610
I share my unstoppable curiosity with you.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:17.410
I'm still able to run through the fog...

00:00:17.510 --> 00:00:21.100
...because I know that you're here for me.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:28.830
I guess the shape of happiness is different for everyone...

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:33.170
...however, I know it's boring when I'm alone...

00:00:33.590 --> 00:00:35.050
But, with you...

00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:37.167
...it's like a mystery!

00:00:38.970 --> 00:00:42.720
It's an enchanting future, where...

00:00:42.890 --> 00:00:47.440
...in order for me to be strong, it's always you...

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:51.820
...that I can continue to depend on, right?

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.400
Just to survive!

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:55.360
Stumped Q? Don't lose your way!

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.200
Take this moment...

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.820
...to fix your gaze and charge on ahead!

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.030
Eternally, we'll always be together...

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.870
...searching and pursuing...

00:01:04.870 --> 00:01:08.580
...the meaning of it all.

00:01:08.580 --> 00:01:10.710
Truth is nothing but a labyrinth...

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.420
...that we try to continue through...

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:16.090
...especially when we are hurt.

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.295
I'll take you, so come this way.

00:01:18.298 --> 00:01:20.090
I'm certain that, on that day...

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:24.010
...I'll see your smile, face to face!

00:01:32.237 --> 00:01:36.074
DDS received a request to investigate
Kamikakushi village...

00:01:36.407 --> 00:01:39.160
...where in the last decade, seven
people have gone missing.

00:01:39.285 --> 00:01:42.914
We, the five members of Q Class, were
dispatched to lead the investigation.

00:01:48.086 --> 00:01:50.046
My butt hurts from all that sitting.

00:01:50.380 --> 00:01:51.965
I'm not getting a signal again.

00:01:52.507 --> 00:01:55.301
We have to walk from here to our lodge
in Hyoutan village, don't we?

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:56.469
That's right.

00:01:59.931 --> 00:02:02.350
I've heard that you need to walk
through a long tunnel...

00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:04.727
...to get from Hyoutan village
to Kamikakushi village.

00:02:04.978 --> 00:02:07.146
Wow, good job finding that out.

00:02:07.438 --> 00:02:09.983
These villages are too small to be in guidebooks.

00:02:10.692 --> 00:02:14.487
I found out a lot about them too,
using my own search engine.

00:02:14.904 --> 00:02:15.572
Like what?

00:02:16.114 --> 00:02:21.411
Because of their weird religion and legends of an old
Japanese army treasure in Kamikakushi village...

00:02:22.078 --> 00:02:24.747
...it's become quite famous on the net now.

00:02:25.415 --> 00:02:27.375
Religion and treasure?

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:32.797
The religion is called Ekishin and they worship
Ekigami, a god that governs epidemic diseases.

00:02:33.047 --> 00:02:36.134
It all dates back to the end of World War II.

00:02:37.802 --> 00:02:38.553
Ekigami?

00:02:39.053 --> 00:02:41.598
I read in the papers that because
of the occult boom...

00:02:41.598 --> 00:02:45.143
...a lot of young people have recently moved to the village.

00:02:46.019 --> 00:02:47.937
Apparently, the missing college student...

00:02:47.937 --> 00:02:51.024
...came here as part of an activity
for his "tore han" club.

00:02:51.441 --> 00:02:52.108
Training pants?

00:02:52.275 --> 00:02:53.234
It's "tore han"!

00:02:53.776 --> 00:02:55.153
Treasure Hunting.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.030
It means searching for treasure.

00:02:57.655 --> 00:03:03.411
Then let's say that we're those "training pants" as
well; that would make the investigation easier.

00:03:03.912 --> 00:03:06.998
I see, that might be the right thing to do.

00:03:08.207 --> 00:03:12.211
We're dealing with someone that gets rid of a person
and calls it a "mysterious disappearance".

00:03:13.254 --> 00:03:15.924
If they figure out that we're
investigating their secret...

00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.678
...this time one of us might disappear.

00:03:31.064 --> 00:03:33.900
Hyoutan village is beyond this tunnel.

00:03:34.233 --> 00:03:35.443
Yeah, let's go.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.408
This tunnel's quite long.

00:03:42.951 --> 00:03:46.371
It's a perfect fit for a village where scary stuff
like the mysterious disappearances occur.

00:03:47.288 --> 00:03:50.166
Will we find a demon? A dark lord?

00:03:51.709 --> 00:03:53.962
No matter what, bring it on!

00:03:54.921 --> 00:03:55.672
There's the exit.

00:03:56.381 --> 00:03:59.842
Now we're finally here, and this is...

00:04:06.307 --> 00:04:08.267
Welcome to Hyoutan village?

00:04:09.018 --> 00:04:10.812
This is kind of disappointing.

00:04:11.396 --> 00:04:12.063
Let's go.

00:04:15.566 --> 00:04:17.568
This is a really peaceful village.

00:04:18.403 --> 00:04:20.655
The name itself is pretty laid back.

00:04:22.991 --> 00:04:25.118
They're selling gourds! Maybe I'll buy one.

00:04:25.284 --> 00:04:27.662
You idiot, This isn't a field trip!

00:04:29.080 --> 00:04:30.540
That's the inn we're staying at tonight.

00:04:31.124 --> 00:04:32.166
Ugh, what a dump.

00:04:32.709 --> 00:04:34.919
Oh, it's good! It has a mysterious flair to it.

00:04:36.212 --> 00:04:37.213
Hello.

00:04:38.589 --> 00:04:40.008
Is anyone home?

00:04:47.932 --> 00:04:49.392
I guess nobody's home.

00:05:03.573 --> 00:05:04.615
That was great.

00:05:04.657 --> 00:05:05.950
They were really afraid.

00:05:06.284 --> 00:05:07.577
W-What?

00:05:10.163 --> 00:05:13.499
Sorry, we didn't think that you'd be that scared.

00:05:17.962 --> 00:05:22.383
What are you saying? You were really
into it too, Iwashimizu-san.

00:05:22.925 --> 00:05:24.969
Hey, Oowada-Chan, turn off the camera.

00:05:26.095 --> 00:05:27.305
Yes, Anzai-san.

00:05:29.599 --> 00:05:32.643
Director Anzai, were you filming this right now?

00:05:33.227 --> 00:05:34.771
Just in case, just in case.

00:05:35.188 --> 00:05:39.984
I mean, if there's no treasure, we have to
deliver something or we'll be in trouble.

00:05:40.151 --> 00:05:43.237
Excuse me, are you from a TV studio?

00:05:43.654 --> 00:05:47.909
Ah, that's right. We're making a show
called "Treasure Adventure".

00:05:48.534 --> 00:05:50.244
You probably don't know it
because it's a little show.

00:05:50.745 --> 00:05:52.330
Are you filming me? Can you see me?

00:05:52.705 --> 00:05:53.539
Hey now...

00:05:53.956 --> 00:05:56.751
Say, say. What are you guys here for?

00:05:56.751 --> 00:05:57.460
The treasure?

00:05:57.460 --> 00:05:58.211
The Ekishin religion?

00:05:58.503 --> 00:05:59.670
Cut it out already!

00:06:01.339 --> 00:06:04.092
Those holy masks are not toys!

00:06:05.384 --> 00:06:07.678
Oh, excuse us, sir.

00:06:08.012 --> 00:06:11.599
These masks made such an impact
that we wanted to give them a try.

00:06:12.475 --> 00:06:18.231
Even people from Hyoutan village can't enter
Kamikakushi village without those masks.

00:06:18.689 --> 00:06:20.691
That's the old tradition.

00:06:21.442 --> 00:06:24.237
If you are going to use them for
your jokes, I'll take them back!

00:06:25.238 --> 00:06:26.280
T-That would be...

00:06:26.447 --> 00:06:29.826
Please don't get so upset. This could be
an advertisement for your inn as well.

00:06:30.201 --> 00:06:33.538
I don't want any more greedy idiots coming here!

00:06:35.081 --> 00:06:40.670
Bah, charging us such high fees for such a
decrepit inn, who are you to call us greedy?

00:06:41.087 --> 00:06:43.464
Well, let's go back to our rooms and
discuss our plans for tomorrow.

00:06:43.589 --> 00:06:44.298
Okay!
Okay!

00:06:46.551 --> 00:06:49.053
Welcome to our humble inn.

00:06:49.428 --> 00:06:52.431
This is Touyalma-sama‘s and
Narusawa-sama‘s room.

00:06:52.598 --> 00:06:55.268
Over there is for Minami-sama, and in the back...

00:06:55.309 --> 00:06:56.686
...is the room for Ryu and me, right?

00:06:57.311 --> 00:07:04.068
If you need anything, please don't
hesitate to ask me or Mio-Chan.

00:07:05.486 --> 00:07:06.487
Certainly!

00:07:06.821 --> 00:07:09.907
Mio-san, you're about our age, aren't you?

00:07:10.324 --> 00:07:15.538
Yes, she's only 17 but she works
instead of going to school.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.291
She's never been outside the village.

00:07:19.167 --> 00:07:20.168
Really?

00:07:20.501 --> 00:07:22.795
Wow, that's quite something.

00:07:23.045 --> 00:07:25.673
You're a year younger than me
and you're already working.

00:07:26.007 --> 00:07:26.883
It's not really a big deal.

00:07:30.469 --> 00:07:32.722
I-I'll so clean the dining hall!

00:07:35.641 --> 00:07:37.018
Well, enjoy your stay.

00:07:38.728 --> 00:07:40.479
What was that about?

00:07:40.897 --> 00:07:44.525
Well, you see, Ryu has a pretty face...

00:07:44.859 --> 00:07:47.737
It was probably that sideways glance that
you with your squinty eyes can't do.

00:07:51.115 --> 00:07:53.367
Wow, what a rundown room...

00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:55.912
The tatami mats are warped...

00:07:56.329 --> 00:07:58.831
It's even worse than Megu's or Kinta's room.

00:08:02.168 --> 00:08:02.877
Say, Kyuu...

00:08:04.045 --> 00:08:05.713
...what do you think about those masks?

00:08:06.380 --> 00:08:09.592
Hmm, they had kind of a gross design.

00:08:09.967 --> 00:08:10.885
Those marks...

00:08:11.844 --> 00:08:13.137
That was smallpox.

00:08:13.804 --> 00:08:14.680
Smallpox?

00:08:15.598 --> 00:08:18.851
It's a highly contagious disease
that's over 2000 years old.

00:08:19.894 --> 00:08:26.275
You develop small, pus-filled blisters over your entire
body. It had an almost 50% mortality rate.

00:08:27.944 --> 00:08:30.780
It was proclaimed to be eradicated in 1980...

00:08:31.948 --> 00:08:35.743
...but it's rumored that it's still being researched
for biological weapon purposes.

00:08:36.369 --> 00:08:38.329
It's the strongest and most lethal virus out there.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:41.332
Why would you make a mask with that stuff?

00:08:43.042 --> 00:08:47.922
It might be a religion that claims that the spreading
of a contagious disease is an act of god.

00:08:49.006 --> 00:08:52.176
That kid pf belief in cursed gods
exists all over the world.

00:08:54.845 --> 00:08:58.641
But what's the point? An epidemic
here in the middle of nowhere...

00:08:59.892 --> 00:09:03.938
Don't these contagious diseases spread
where there's a lot of people?

00:09:04.397 --> 00:09:07.066
You're right, this place is full of strange things.

00:09:09.277 --> 00:09:11.946
The legend of the treasures that the
old Japanese army left behind...

00:09:12.655 --> 00:09:15.074
...the Ekishin religion that wears
those strange masks...

00:09:15.491 --> 00:09:19.370
...and the mysterious disappearance
in Kamikakushi village.

00:09:22.498 --> 00:09:26.627
Okay, now that we're all here, let's go over
our investigation plans for tomorrow.

00:09:27.211 --> 00:09:29.380
According to the data from school...

00:09:29.714 --> 00:09:31.924
...the missing college student was staying...

00:09:32.049 --> 00:09:37.054
...at the Kamikakushi branch of the
Ryouzanpaku Inn on the other side of the tunnel.

00:09:38.097 --> 00:09:39.682
Then let's all go there tomorrow.

00:09:39.765 --> 00:09:40.474
Alright!

00:09:40.516 --> 00:09:41.684
I don't think we can do that.

00:09:42.018 --> 00:09:46.439
You need to be wearing those masks
to enter Kamikakushi village.

00:09:47.732 --> 00:09:52.111
Since the TV crew has already borrowed
some masks from this inn...

00:09:52.528 --> 00:09:54.447
...there are only two left.

00:09:55.072 --> 00:09:57.116
Then how about borrowing them
from the people in the area?

00:09:57.366 --> 00:10:00.119
I thought about that and asked
Mio-san earlier, but...

00:10:01.454 --> 00:10:02.413
That's impossible.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:05.624
Every household really values their masks.

00:10:05.875 --> 00:10:09.462
They say that you will become cursed if
you give out your household's mask.

00:10:10.379 --> 00:10:13.007
That means we can't get any more masks.

00:10:13.924 --> 00:10:18.471
Then how about sneaking by a different
route without using masks?

00:10:18.554 --> 00:10:19.513
That wont work.

00:10:21.849 --> 00:10:23.809
...Hyoutan village and Kamikakushi village...

00:10:23.851 --> 00:10:27.104
...are two solitary islands of flat
land surrounded by steep cliffs.

00:10:27.772 --> 00:10:29.774
You can only get in through the tunnel.

00:10:32.109 --> 00:10:33.277
Let's split up into two groups.

00:10:34.653 --> 00:10:38.949
Two of us will borrow the remaining masks
and go to Kamikakushi village.

00:10:39.825 --> 00:10:40.910
That's the only way, isn't it?

00:10:41.452 --> 00:10:42.953
But, which two?

00:10:43.412 --> 00:10:45.206
Raise your hand if you want to go.

00:10:47.917 --> 00:10:49.001
<i>Just the two of us...</i>

00:10:51.420 --> 00:10:52.630
<i>will go to Kamikakushi village".</i>

00:10:53.672 --> 00:10:56.384
<i>even though there might be
a murderer hiding there,</i>

00:10:57.385 --> 00:10:58.886
<i>It's too dangerous,</i>

00:11:00.471 --> 00:11:01.889
I would definitely like to go.

00:11:02.348 --> 00:11:03.057
Ryu-kun...

00:11:03.808 --> 00:11:09.522
Truthfully, I have my concerns with only
two going into that creepy village...

00:11:10.439 --> 00:11:15.403
...but, the drive to find the truth is even stronger.

00:11:18.489 --> 00:11:21.367
The drive to find the truth...

00:11:22.284 --> 00:11:25.996
I can't become a detective if I'm
scared by something like this.

00:11:27.706 --> 00:11:30.501
That's right, if a detective gives up, a
case will remain unsolved forever.

00:11:30.793 --> 00:11:31.544
I'm going!

00:11:31.836 --> 00:11:32.628
I'm going too!

00:11:32.837 --> 00:11:33.671
Me too.

00:11:34.255 --> 00:11:35.089
I'll go too.

00:11:35.548 --> 00:11:37.466
Very well, we decide by lottery.

00:11:42.596 --> 00:11:45.766
There's two burned matches in here.

00:11:46.434 --> 00:11:48.978
The ones that get those will
go to Kamikjakushi village.

00:11:49.687 --> 00:11:50.396
It that okay?

00:11:53.649 --> 00:11:55.317
Then on three we all take one.

00:11:56.026 --> 00:11:57.153
One, two, three!

00:12:02.199 --> 00:12:04.535
This outside bath is quite nice.

00:12:04.827 --> 00:12:05.953
It really is.

00:12:06.162 --> 00:12:07.997
Last time we were here to check out this place...

00:12:07.997 --> 00:12:11.834
...we couldn't really relax because of that
ruckus about the missing college student.

00:12:12.293 --> 00:12:15.421
I don't intend to relax this time either.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:19.175
I mean if we find the treasures
of the old Japanese army...

00:12:19.383 --> 00:12:23.179
...the finders get half of it.

00:12:23.804 --> 00:12:29.059
Then ”I quit being a poor director and
move to Hawaii and live "aloha style".

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:32.313
You're dreaming again, aren't you.

00:12:32.521 --> 00:12:34.440
It's not a dream.

00:12:34.899 --> 00:12:35.774
Azcgami-Chan?

00:12:36.567 --> 00:12:42.114
I heard that the missing college student
knew something about the treasure.

00:12:42.406 --> 00:12:43.616
Right, Kagami-san?

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:47.578
Uh, well. I don't really know too much about it.

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:52.291
What are you talking about? You were
the first one to find that footprint.

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:56.837
You and one of the college student's
friends went into his room as well.

00:12:57.171 --> 00:13:00.174
Is that true, Kagami? Why did
you keep quiet about it?

00:13:00.841 --> 00:13:01.926
I-I'm sorry...

00:13:02.426 --> 00:13:05.930
It didn't have anything to do with the
show and I was kind of scared.

00:13:06.764 --> 00:13:10.559
Well, I actually have something nice too.

00:13:10.976 --> 00:13:11.685
Something nice?

00:13:12.436 --> 00:13:13.521
A photo.

00:13:14.271 --> 00:13:17.399
A photo of a note the college student left.

00:13:17.900 --> 00:13:20.528
I bought it off his friends at the time.

00:13:21.695 --> 00:13:23.364
You're an impossible woman.

00:13:23.781 --> 00:13:24.990
What's in the note?

00:13:25.533 --> 00:13:26.700
That's my secret...

00:13:28.327 --> 00:13:30.871
I mean we're all rivals in this treasure hunt.

00:13:39.338 --> 00:13:41.173
Oh, Ryou, it's me.

00:13:42.049 --> 00:13:44.885
Tomorrow that TV team will be going over there.

00:13:45.511 --> 00:13:49.265
And twp of those five young kids too.

00:13:49.682 --> 00:13:52.601
Yes, Father. Is it another treasure hunt?

00:13:53.435 --> 00:13:58.023
Yes, scare them off as usual.

00:13:58.566 --> 00:14:00.526
Yes, understood.

00:14:09.535 --> 00:14:11.453
Ah, it's so cool out here.

00:14:18.294 --> 00:14:21.130
I'll definitely get the treasure.

00:14:21.714 --> 00:14:27.136
Now then, I need to wake up early
tomorrow and confirm "that".

00:14:41.399 --> 00:14:43.860
A meal after a good night of sleep is so good.

00:14:44.778 --> 00:14:46.071
Right, Megu?

00:14:50.367 --> 00:14:52.202
Then on three we all take one.

00:14:52.828 --> 00:14:53.829
One, two, three!

00:14:58.708 --> 00:15:00.836
M-Megu and Ryu got them.

00:15:00.836 --> 00:15:03.255
Damn, I can't believe I lost.

00:15:03.964 --> 00:15:07.050
I guess it's decided that Ryu-kun and Mega
are going to Kamikakushi village.

00:15:09.511 --> 00:15:10.971
Let's do this, Megu.

00:15:12.931 --> 00:15:15.642
Y-Yeah, Ryu-kun.

00:15:18.937 --> 00:15:20.188
Why are you blushing?

00:15:20.814 --> 00:15:22.566
I'm not blushing.

00:15:23.441 --> 00:15:24.067
Good morning.

00:15:24.568 --> 00:15:25.777
G-Good morning.

00:15:26.736 --> 00:15:27.904
She blushed again!
She blushed again!

00:15:28.155 --> 00:15:29.531
No I didn't!

00:15:29.656 --> 00:15:31.741
Hey, why didn't you say that earlier?

00:15:31.825 --> 00:15:34.452
I'm sorry, I thought she was with one of you...

00:15:34.828 --> 00:15:35.704
They're having an argument,
You idiot!

00:15:36.246 --> 00:15:37.747
I wonder what happened.
As the producer...

00:15:38.707 --> 00:15:42.961
...I'm responsible if something
happens to my staff!

00:15:43.587 --> 00:15:44.963
In any case, so look for her!

00:15:45.255 --> 00:15:46.006
Yes sir.

00:15:46.590 --> 00:15:49.134
Excuse me, AD-san, did something happen?

00:15:49.634 --> 00:15:51.011
Oh, well...

00:15:51.553 --> 00:15:56.850
Our reporter, Azegami-san, didn't come
back after getting out of the bath.

00:15:58.768 --> 00:15:59.728
She was spirited away.

00:16:02.772 --> 00:16:08.195
Everybody that comes here for the
treasure hunt gets spirited away.

00:16:09.112 --> 00:16:10.655
T-That couldn't be...

00:16:11.531 --> 00:16:12.199
Umm...

00:16:13.158 --> 00:16:14.743
There might have been an incident.

00:16:15.493 --> 00:16:16.828
Let's look for your reporter.

00:16:18.079 --> 00:16:19.414
Hey, Kyuu...

00:16:19.789 --> 00:16:22.042
What? Who are you guys?

00:16:23.376 --> 00:16:28.423
Ah, we're just, uh...

00:16:29.466 --> 00:16:31.134
...a detective club!

00:16:32.761 --> 00:16:35.972
I thought we said we were going
to be treasure hunters...

00:16:36.139 --> 00:16:37.557
You're not weird then...

00:16:37.807 --> 00:16:38.767
well

00:16:40.894 --> 00:16:44.022
Sir, that sickle. It's the one
you had yesterday, right?

00:16:45.065 --> 00:16:47.484
Its blade is chipped in the same place and...

00:16:49.361 --> 00:16:51.696
Wow, you've got a good memory.

00:16:51.988 --> 00:16:54.157
But what about it?

00:16:54.491 --> 00:16:58.453
- Well, yesterday it was covered
in mud, and now it's clean.

00:16:58.787 --> 00:17:00.538
So it kind of bugged me.

00:17:01.206 --> 00:17:04.042
Normally you don't really wash sickles, right?

00:17:07.754 --> 00:17:11.549
I don't remember washing
it, but it really is clean...

00:17:12.926 --> 00:17:14.594
Sir may I?

00:17:18.765 --> 00:17:19.766
That's the smell of blood.

00:17:22.185 --> 00:17:24.145
What are you guys trying to say?

00:17:26.189 --> 00:17:28.066
That someone...

00:17:28.984 --> 00:17:30.652
...after stabbing someone else with that sickle...

00:17:31.611 --> 00:17:34.406
...unintentionally washed the mud away
as they cleaned off the blood.

00:17:35.407 --> 00:17:37.993
We're saying that this is a possibility.

00:17:38.743 --> 00:17:39.619
You gotta be joking.

00:17:41.204 --> 00:17:43.498
Sir, where was the sickle stored?

00:17:45.709 --> 00:17:49.462
Oh, it was behind the outdoor baths,
stuck into one of the bushes.

00:17:50.964 --> 00:17:54.467
It was here. I stuck in here like this.

00:17:55.302 --> 00:17:57.929
If someone got stabbed with a sickle...

00:17:58.596 --> 00:18:00.098
...there should be a lot of blood around here.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.894
But it's hard to see anything
because this is a dirt floor.

00:18:05.895 --> 00:18:09.399
Don't worry, that's what we have Kinta for.

00:18:10.025 --> 00:18:12.068
Now Kinta, get down there and sniff around.

00:18:12.652 --> 00:18:14.279
I'm not a police dog!

00:18:14.571 --> 00:18:15.697
Like I could tell!

00:18:16.197 --> 00:18:19.200
You ,were bragging that your sense
of smell was as good as a dog's.

00:18:19.826 --> 00:18:21.369
I didn't mean that literally!

00:18:21.828 --> 00:18:22.704
Oh well...

00:18:24.247 --> 00:18:25.999
...could I borrow your first aid kit?

00:18:27.375 --> 00:18:28.960
Sure, but what do you need?

00:18:29.461 --> 00:18:34.257
I have. a good way to find traces
of large amounts of blood.

00:18:37.260 --> 00:18:38.720
Ah, here is it.

00:18:39.679 --> 00:18:40.722
Oxydol?

00:18:41.139 --> 00:18:42.390
What are you going to do with that?

00:18:44.267 --> 00:18:46.311
Um, is this alright?

00:18:46.519 --> 00:18:48.104
Yeah, thanks Mio-san.

00:18:55.487 --> 00:18:56.738
Should be around here I think...

00:18:56.946 --> 00:18:58.198
Hey, what are you doing?

00:18:58.656 --> 00:19:00.533
What will happen to the trees
in the yard if you do that?

00:19:05.163 --> 00:19:05.955
I see!

00:19:06.706 --> 00:19:11.378
Oxydol reacts with the catalase
in blood and releases oxygen.

00:19:12.337 --> 00:19:15.757
Its the same reaction you see when
you apply oxydol to a wound.

00:19:16.716 --> 00:19:22.097
Basically, this means that there is a
large amount of blood in this dirt.

00:19:23.932 --> 00:19:24.808
Which means...

00:19:24.974 --> 00:19:26.935
Hey, don't be joking around!

00:19:26.935 --> 00:19:28.395
Look at this!

00:19:29.813 --> 00:19:30.522
Kinta?

00:19:31.106 --> 00:19:37.028
This is a tire track of one of those wheelbarrows you
use at construction sites to transport heavy things.

00:19:38.655 --> 00:19:41.449
The perpetrator might have used
it to transport the corpse.

00:19:57.048 --> 00:19:58.174
It stops here...

00:19:58.883 --> 00:20:03.221
Which means that it couldn't
have been carried too far.

00:20:03.805 --> 00:20:06.266
That means she's buried somewhere
around here.

00:20:10.603 --> 00:20:15.567
This is no good, there's no way we can
dig up every field around here.

00:20:16.025 --> 00:20:21.322
The body won’t be in any of the fields because you
don't know when it might be dug up by a tractor.

00:20:22.866 --> 00:20:28.413
If I were the perpetrator, there's only
one good place to hide the body.

00:20:29.289 --> 00:20:30.081
Over there!

00:20:35.044 --> 00:20:36.588
This is a pretty old graveyard.

00:20:38.756 --> 00:20:42.427
Sir, burial is still the tradition
around here, right?

00:20:42.844 --> 00:20:43.511
Yeah.

00:20:43.803 --> 00:20:44.637
Burial?

00:20:47.474 --> 00:20:50.727
If the perpetrator buried the
corpse in an old grave...

00:20:51.644 --> 00:20:53.813
...it normally wouldn't be dug up again.

00:20:56.691 --> 00:20:57.317
Look!

00:20:57.400 --> 00:20:58.818
look, this one has been disturbed.

00:21:03.281 --> 00:21:06.075
You're right, the dirt looks fresh.

00:21:11.372 --> 00:21:12.165
Let's dig it up.

00:21:12.832 --> 00:21:14.959
Hey, you'll be cursed if you do that...

00:21:15.668 --> 00:21:19.297
What if the body was buried
here because of that belief?

00:21:20.340 --> 00:21:22.133
Alright, I‘ll dig it up.

00:21:22.383 --> 00:21:23.259
Kurozumi-san...

00:21:23.676 --> 00:21:24.761
We'll help too.

00:21:25.303 --> 00:21:26.346
Kagami, get some shovels!

00:21:26.679 --> 00:21:27.388
Yes, sir.

00:21:48.201 --> 00:21:49.786
There it is, the coffin's lid...

00:21:50.828 --> 00:21:51.496
Alright.

00:22:09.556 --> 00:22:12.433
It looks like she wasn't spirited away.

00:22:13.977 --> 00:22:15.812
This is a murder.

00:22:17.981 --> 00:22:18.481
Hmm?

00:22:19.107 --> 00:22:20.191
She's holding something.

00:22:22.902 --> 00:22:24.904
Judging from the scratch wounds...

00:22:25.822 --> 00:22:27.865
...I think the perpetrator tried to get this.

00:22:28.408 --> 00:22:29.659
Hey, Ryu...

00:22:30.326 --> 00:22:31.578
This is "infi".

00:22:32.537 --> 00:22:33.663
The sign for infinity.

00:22:33.955 --> 00:22:34.581
Gimme that.

00:22:36.291 --> 00:22:40.753
So this is that missing student's note
that Azegami was talking about.

00:22:41.504 --> 00:22:43.089
There's no doubt about that.

00:22:44.799 --> 00:22:45.800
This is amazing.

00:22:46.050 --> 00:22:48.803
Even though Azegami was
killed because of this...

00:22:49.220 --> 00:22:52.932
...the legend about the treasures of the
old Japanese army might be true!

00:22:53.308 --> 00:22:55.476
Now I'm definitely going to look into this further.

00:22:55.643 --> 00:22:57.604
What kind of people are they?

00:22:58.354 --> 00:23:00.064
Talking like that right off
corpse of their friend.

00:23:01.649 --> 00:23:03.318
That was the anger of Ekigami-sama.

00:23:06.029 --> 00:23:06.821
Who are you?

00:23:13.995 --> 00:23:15.705
Ryou, you're back.

00:23:16.039 --> 00:23:17.040
Yes, Father.

00:23:20.668 --> 00:23:23.671
There has been a divine message
from the high priest.

00:23:24.756 --> 00:23:26.424
"This is only the beginning."

00:23:28.217 --> 00:23:29.927
That's what the message
from Ekigami-sama said.

00:23:37.250 --> 00:23:40.503
The Sun is setting in a red glow...

00:23:41.088 --> 00:23:43.591
...as it follows me.

00:23:43.955 --> 00:23:46.764
Along this deserted beach...

00:23:46.767 --> 00:23:50.693
...I walk alone once more.

00:23:50.706 --> 00:23:54.075
I can't continue to hold in...

00:23:54.737 --> 00:23:57.090
...the tears that should pour out.

00:23:57.720 --> 00:24:00.167
Why have these memories...

00:24:00.169 --> 00:24:03.699
...become so wonderful?

00:24:04.270 --> 00:24:09.266
Ah... Like an ocean wave, I return to you...

00:24:09.516 --> 00:24:12.039
...because I'm so in love.

00:24:12.770 --> 00:24:15.756
And, now my heart...

00:24:15.761 --> 00:24:17.919
...is heavy with pain.

00:24:18.854 --> 00:24:21.794
Reflections of a bright rainbow...

00:24:21.927 --> 00:24:26.057
...shine on the distant shores of yesterday.

00:24:26.397 --> 00:24:30.028
I'll never forget those days...

00:24:30.035 --> 00:24:35.143
...and I long to see you again.

00:24:37.238 --> 00:24:41.075
Each member of Q Class sets out to reveal
the truth about Kamikakushi village.

00:24:41.408 --> 00:24:45.829
Ryu and Megu head for the village interior and Kazuma
discovers the cipher for the legend of the treasure.

00:24:46.372 --> 00:24:49.875
But a second case occurs in front of our eyes...

00:24:50.626 --> 00:24:53.712
That was a mysterious disappearance that can
only be thought of as another spiriting away.

00:24:54.505 --> 00:24:55.673
There's only one answer!

00:24:57.591 --> 00:24:58.467
Its me, Nanami.

00:24:59.009 --> 00:25:03.889
This is a bit sudden, but did you see that I had
disguised myself as a cactus in the main episode?

00:25:04.390 --> 00:25:05.182
The answer is...

00:25:08.394 --> 00:25:11.105
I'll be hiding next week too, so good luck!
